<% title "What kind of business?" %>

<% content_for :progress, 10 %>

<%# FUIME: the three-card fork and the service picker, ahead of describing the
    business.

    Modelled on Whop's new-business onboarding, with its third card deliberately
    changed. Whop offers "clone a proven business"; that requires holding real
    operators up as proven, and ranking operators is what MOR_MIGRATION_PLAN
    §8.3 D2 forbids — the same reasoning that made /directory a listing rather
    than a dispatch. A Fuime-authored template names nobody and ranks nothing.

    Nothing on this page suggests a price. See Fuime::ServiceCatalog for why that
    is a constraint rather than an omission, and
    spec/lib/fuime/service_catalog_spec.rb for the check that keeps it true. %>

<% content_for :info_pane do %>
  <div class="flex flex-col">
    <h2 class="text-4xl">What kind of business?</h2>
    <p class="mt-0 text-lg muted">
      Two quick questions, then we'll get to the details.
    </p>

    <%# The launch scope, said plainly rather than discovered at vetting. L8's
        failure mode is the site describing a product that does not exist, and a
        picker showing categories the app then blocks is that in miniature. %>
    <%# Fuime: this said "services only, digital downloads coming later", which
        stopped being true when Fuime::OperatorEligibility::ELIGIBLE_CATEGORIES
        gained `digital` and the catalog gained templates that resolve to it.
        Copy that closes a door the app has opened is the same L8 failure as
        copy that opens one the app has closed — it just costs a founder a
        template instead of costing Fuime a promise. Physical goods and food
        really are still shut, so those stay named. %>
    <div class="card card--outline mt-6">
      <h3 class="text-base mt-0 mb-1">What you can sell today</h3>
      <p class="text-sm muted mb-0">
        Services — work you do for someone — and digital things you make, like a
        design, an edit, or a small piece of software. Physical products and food
        are coming later.
      </p>
    </div>

    <%# The same ten templates, in full, for somebody who does not yet know what
        to pick. /learn is public, so this link works before and after sign-up. %>
    <div class="mt-4">
      <p class="text-sm muted mb-0">
        Not sure yet?
        <%= link_to "Browse all the starter templates", learn_path(anchor: "templates"),
                    target: "_blank", rel: "noopener", class: "underline" %> —
        each one covers what to offer, where the first customers come from, and
        what tends to go wrong. Your application is saved; you won't lose it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
<% end %>

<%= form_with model: @application,
              url: application_path(@application, return_to: project_info_application_path(@application)),
              method: :patch,
              id: "edit_application_#{@application.id}",
              class: "mt-7" do |form| %>

  <%# ── Question one: where are you starting from ───────────────────────── %>
  <div class="card card--outline mb-6">
    <%= form.label :starting_point do %>
      Where are you starting from? <span class="text-primary">*</span>
    <% end %>
    <p class="text-sm muted mt-1 mb-3">There's no wrong answer — it just changes what we show you next.</p>

    <div class="field field--options max-w-none mb-0 relative">
      <% @starting_points.each do |point| %>
        <%= form.radio_button :starting_point, point.key,
                              { checked: @application.starting_point == point.key,
                                required: true,
                                class: "absolute !block opacity-0"
} %>
        <%= form.label :starting_point, value: point.key do %>
          <strong><%= point.name %></strong>
          <small><%= point.blurb %></small>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </div>

  <%# ── Question two: what do you do ────────────────────────────────────── %>
  <div class="card card--outline mb-6">
    <%= form.label :service_type do %>
      What do you do? <span class="text-primary">*</span>
    <% end %>
    <p class="text-sm muted mt-1 mb-3">
      Pick the closest one. You'll describe it in your own words on the next page.
    </p>

    <%= form.select :service_type,
                    options_for_select(@services.map { |s| [s.name, s.key] }, @application.service_type),
                    { include_blank: "Choose a service…" },
                    { class: "w-full max-w-full", required: true } %>

    <%# The checklist for whichever service is selected. Rendered for all of them
        and revealed by the picker rather than fetched, because the whole catalog
        is a few hundred bytes and a round-trip per selection would make the page
        feel slower than the question deserves. %>
    <% @services.each do |service| %>
      <div class="mt-4" data-service-checklist="<%= service.key %>"
           style="<%= "display: none;" unless @application.service_type == service.key %>">
        <p class="text-sm mb-1"><strong><%= service.name %></strong> — <%= service.blurb %></p>
        <p class="text-sm muted mb-1">Worth deciding before your first customer:</p>
        <ul class="text-sm muted mb-0 pl-4">
          <% service.checklist.each do |item| %>
            <li><%= item %></li>
          <% end %>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-sm mb-0 mt-2">
          <%= link_to "Read the full #{service.name.downcase} template →",
                      learn_template_path(slug: service.key),
                      target: "_blank", rel: "noopener", class: "underline" %>
        </p>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </div>
<% end %>

<%# No build step and no Stimulus controller for six lines of show/hide. The
    page works without it — every checklist would simply render — so this is
    progressive enhancement rather than a dependency. %>
<script>
  (function () {
    var picker = document.getElementById("event_application_service_type");
    if (!picker) return;

    function sync() {
      document.querySelectorAll("[data-service-checklist]").forEach(function (el) {
        el.style.display = el.dataset.serviceChecklist === picker.value ? "" : "none";
      });
    }

    picker.addEventListener("change", sync);
    sync();
  })();
</script>

<% content_for :footer do %>
  <div class="flex items-center justify-start gap-4">
    <%= responsive_link_to applications_path, text: "Back to dashboard", icon: "view-back", class: "btn bg-muted" %>
  </div>
  <button class="btn bg-blue" form="edit_application_<%= @application.id %>">Continue</button>
<% end %>
